  <!-- SPECIES / TAXONOMY -->
  <section class="taxonomy-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-hd">
        <div class="t disp">Six species — one family</div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Genus Orthoebolavirus</span>
      </div>
      <div class="taxon-grid">
        <div class="taxon" style="border-top:2px solid var(--severe)">
          <div class="sp">Orthoebolavirus zairense</div>
          <div class="abbr">EBOV · Zaire</div>
          <div class="meta">The original and most-studied species. Caused the 2014–16 West Africa catastrophe and the 2018–20 Kivu outbreak — the two largest in history. The only Ebola with a licensed vaccine (Ervebo) and approved treatments (mAb114, REGN-EB3).</div>
          <div class="cfr-bar"><div class="cfr-fill" style="width:75%;background:var(--severe)"></div></div>
          <div class="cfr-val">CFR range ~60–90% · untreated</div>
        </div>
        <div class="taxon" style="border-top:2px solid var(--watch)">
          <div class="sp">Orthoebolavirus sudanense</div>
          <div class="abbr">SUDV · Sudan</div>
          <div class="meta">First detected simultaneously with Zaire virus in 1976 but in Sudan, 850 km away. Lower CFR but recurs in Uganda. No licensed vaccine. The 2022 Mubende outbreak — no Ervebo, no mAb treatment — reminded the field how vulnerable SUDV leaves patients.</div>
          <div class="cfr-bar"><div class="cfr-fill" style="width:53%;background:var(--watch)"></div></div>
          <div class="cfr-val">CFR range ~41–65% · untreated</div>
        </div>
        <div class="taxon" style="border-top:2px solid var(--contained)">
          <div class="sp">Orthoebolavirus bundibugyoense</div>
          <div class="abbr">BDBV · Bundibugyo</div>
          <div class="meta">Identified in 2007 during an outbreak in western Uganda’s Bundibugyo District. Causes the active 2025–26 PHEIC in DRC and Uganda. Lower CFR than Zaire historically, but no vaccine, no targeted treatment. Current outbreak is only the third known event.</div>
          <div class="cfr-bar"><div class="cfr-fill" style="width:31%;background:var(--contained)"></div></div>
          <div class="cfr-val">CFR ~25–31% · historical range</div>
        </div>
        <div class="taxon" style="border-top:2px solid var(--faint)">
          <div class="sp">Orthoebolavirus taiense</div>
          <div class="abbr">TAFV · Taï Forest</div>
          <div class="meta">A single confirmed human case in 1994 — a scientist who performed a necropsy on an infected chimpanzee in Côte d’Ivoire and survived. No known subsequent human infections. Studied for its phylogenetic relationship to the other species.</div>
          <div class="cfr-bar"><div class="cfr-fill" style="width:0%;background:var(--faint)"></div></div>
          <div class="cfr-val">1 case · 0 deaths · isolated event</div>
        </div>
        <div class="taxon" style="border-top:2px solid var(--faint)">
          <div class="sp">Orthoebolavirus restonense</div>
          <div class="abbr">RESTV · Reston</div>
          <div class="meta">First detected in macaques imported to Reston, Virginia from the Philippines in 1989. Several humans seroconverted but none became ill. Not considered pathogenic to humans. Its presence in Philippine pigs raised questions about an expanded host range.</div>
          <div class="cfr-bar"><div class="cfr-fill" style="width:0%;background:var(--faint)"></div></div>
          <div class="cfr-val">0 human deaths · not pathogenic</div>
        </div>
        <div class="taxon" style="border-top:2px solid var(--faint)">
          <div class="sp">Orthoebolavirus bombaliense</div>
          <div class="abbr">BOMV · Bombali</div>
          <div class="meta">Discovered in Sierra Leone in 2018 in two species of free-tailed bats. No confirmed human infections have ever been documented. Its characterization is ongoing and it remains the least understood of the six species — a reminder that the known range of filovirus diversity may be incomplete.</div>
          <div class="cfr-bar"><div class="cfr-fill" style="width:0%;background:var(--faint)"></div></div>
          <div class="cfr-val">No confirmed human cases · bat reservoir</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

